export anchor InkAndRedStyle:
    number: 295
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Ink and red
    idea: A pull request set like the front page of a serious evening paper, warm white serif type on black ink, hairline column rules and one sharp red kept for what blocks the merge.
    base: dark
    palette:
        inkBlack: #0e0d0c, the page and style sheet ground
        pressBlack: #171614, the diff excerpt box and fields
        warmWhite: #ede7db, text, thick section rules and the secondary button
        greyInk: #aaa397, meta, captions and labels
        hairline: #3b3833, column rules and row lines
        sharpRed: #ff5245, the one accent for failing, changes requested, the primary button, the current tab bar and the focus ring
        redWash: #2a1311, the failing alert and removed diff lines
        redText: #ff8a80, red words set on the red wash and the needs QA label
    type:
        Three families. A high contrast display serif, Didot, Bodoni 72,
        Iowan Old Style, Georgia, for the masthead, headline and big
        figure. A book serif, Iowan Old Style, Palatino, Georgia, for body
        text at 17px and 1.55 and the italic dek at 24px. A gothic sans,
        Franklin Gothic Medium, Arial Narrow, Arial, for kickers and labels
        at 12 to 13px bold caps tracked 0.16em. The headline is 64px at 700,
        the checks figure 76px, the diff 13px monospace.
    layout:
        A centred newspaper page up to 1240px. An ear line names the suite,
        the edition and the desk. The masthead reads Brightwork Code in
        64px display serif with Code in italic, the repository in italic
        below it, and a dateline row with Private, Watch 12, Star 48 and
        Fork 3, closed by a double rule. The tabs are a centred row of
        gothic caps separated by middots, the current one with a 3px red
        underline. The lead story has a red kicker with the number and Open,
        the title as a huge headline, the merge sentence as an italic dek
        and a ruled byline with author, commits, files and totals. Under it
        two columns split by a hairline. The narrow one holds The checks
        with a giant 11 and of 12 passed, a red washed alert for the failing
        e2e-android check, The review with the two names and verdicts, and
        In this change as a contents list with dotted leaders to the
        counts. The wide one holds The excerpt, the boxed diff, where the
        comment becomes a pull quote with a red rule above and the quote in
        26px italic display serif. A right rail under a thick white rule
        lists assignee, labels, milestone and linked issue, then To press
        with the dashed disabled merge button. Below 1060px the rail moves
        under the story, below 760px the columns stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px column gutters, 12px row padding, 28px between masthead and lead.
    density: Medium. Big headlines and long lines, but every fact is on the page.
    corners: None. Every edge is square.
    borders: Hairline column rules, a 3px or 4px warm white rule over every section, a double rule under the masthead.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Few, 2px line icons with butt caps. A tick for passed, an octagon
        cross for failing, a ringed tick for approved, a triangle for
        changes requested, each with its word in gothic caps.
    focus: A 2px warm white outline offset 3px with a 5px red ring outside it.
    tone: Headline voice, such as The checks, The review, The excerpt, In this change and To press.
